rom the given options, the only possible equation is $y={x}^{3}(x+1){(x-2)}^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348374 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348374 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80361" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348374 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348374 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0b/0bf56fdb429d050465875f1c885aa83a36fb4fd7bfe4709fcda11db1a3574a2d.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=-{x}^{4}(x+1)(x-2{)}^{3}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348374 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "33b39cd4-c03b-51ce-be6d-3b47ccd122f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348374 #edb/ref 1074 "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0$ is $4,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=-1$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=-1$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=2$ is $3,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=2$ is a triple-root, the graph must be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{III}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$\n\nOnly graph $\\text{III}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is $\\text{III}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428557 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428557 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 2 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected frac